<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RM_Contagion                        CONTAGION_RM_MOD_BUILD_1, new 2026-09-25

    Copied verbatim from the frozen src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/
    RUT_Contagion.xml (156 lines, authored 2026-09-09) per
    design/RimMandrake/biome_mod_architecture.md §5 Phase A step 2. Every field
    below is the twin's own content, unchanged, EXCEPT:

      - workerClass: the donor AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_OcularForest becomes this
        mod's own RimMandrake.Contagion.RM_BiomeWorker_Contagion (§5 step 2 — a
        donor type in workerClass is a hard dependency the RimMandrake tier may
        not assume). The new worker's placement ranges are [INVENTED], same
        footing as the sibling Abyss/Blue Desert mods' own worker
        ranges — no worldgen run has been done for this mod and the campaign
        world is frozen and hand-authored, so one never will be for Ash'karr.
      - RM_Sytheclaw gains an explicit MayRequire="mandrake.rut.patches": it
        is a RimMandrake-tier creature (not Star Wars) whose ThingDef/
        PawnKindDef still live in the RimUtinni tier
        (RM_PyrelandsPortedFauna.xml), shared inline across three biomes
        (Pyrelands, Greentide, here). Without the gate this def would carry a
        live cross-tier hard dependency the franchise-free RimMandrake tier
        may not assume — same caution WildAnimals_Greentide.xml already
        records for this same creature. `BIOME_SPECIFIC_FAUNA_LAW_1` lists it
        among 52 unadjudicated multi-homed species; multi-home evictions are
        stopped by owner ruling, so it is not moved or renamed here.

    Everything else — texture, terrain, weather, diseases — is the twin's
    content unchanged.

    ⚠️ NOT donor-free: terrain/texture entries carry no MayRequire (inherited
    from the twin, not this build's scope to fix) — see About.xml for the
    disclosure.

    🔧 FIXED 2026-09-29 (CONTAGION_FINAL_BAN_SWEEP_1): the wildPlants row named
    `RUT_RustPuff` with `MayRequire="mandrake.rut.rotsporekit"` — dead on
    arrival. `mandrake.rut.rotsporekit` was absorbed into `mandrake.rm.therot`
    on 2026-09-24 (THEROT_RM_MOD_BUILD_1, `df79753dc`), a day BEFORE this mod
    was built by copying the twin verbatim, and the plant itself was renamed
    `RM_RustPuff` in that same absorption
    (src/RimMandrake/TheRot/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/RM_RotSporeKit_Flora.xml).
    So the row named a defName that has never existed and gated on a
    packageId that no About.xml has ever declared — the entry could never
    resolve and the plant could never spawn here, regardless of TheRot's
    load state. Now `RM_RustPuff` / `MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes"`.
    Other files across the repo still cite the stale `RUT_RustPuff` name —
    out of this mod's scope, left for a separate sweep.

    ⭐ SUPERSEDED 2026-09-29 (CONTAGION_RULED_CONTENT_1 Wave A, then
    CONTAGION_FLORA_PORT_1): every donor AA_/AB_ row and RM_Sytheclaw (never
    admitted; Pyrelands is its home) were replaced outright — <wildAnimals> by
    the 16-def RM_ port in Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RM_ContagionFauna.xml,
    <wildPlants> by the 9-def RM_ port in Defs/PlantDefs/RM_ContagionFlora.xml
    (cast bible §4) — per the cast bible's full-RM-development ruling. Both
    rosters are now donor-free and cross-mod-dependency-free (RUT_RustPuff's
    own dependency above is unrelated: a RUT_ campaign-layer item, not an AB_
    donor row).
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RM_Contagion</defName>
    <label>the Contagion</label>
    <description>A red valley on a scalded mountain, roofed by a thunderstorm that has never been known to stop. Under the cloud everything is wet, warm and unfinished: trees half-way to being something else, animals with one design completed and two abandoned. Then the cloud tears -- and the sun comes through like a sterilizing lamp, and everything alive dives for cover, because here the clear sky is the killer.</description>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.Contagion.RM_BiomeWorker_Contagion</workerClass>
    <lakeBeachTerrain>GU_AlienSandFine</lakeBeachTerrain>
    <mudTerrain>GU_AlienSandFine</mudTerrain>
    <riverbankTerrain>GU_AlienSandFine</riverbankTerrain>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>3.0</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.35</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>Biomes/AB_OcularForest</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>30</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>RM_Disease_SporeAllergy</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>50</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>RM_Disease_AnimalSporeAllergy</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>50</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Malaria</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>160</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SleepingSickness</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>140</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>GU_AlienSandFine</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.2</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>GU_AlienSand</terrain>
        <min>0.2</min>
        <max>0.87</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>GU_RichAlienSand</terrain>
        <min>0.87</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <!-- CONTAGION_MECHANICS_BUILD_1 Part 1 (2026-09-29): the biome owns its
         sky. The Bloom (RM_ContagionBloom, ours) replaces the donor AB_RedFog
         as the standing state. Clear and DryThunderstorm are OUT: here the
         clear sky is the Burn, and the Burn is never rolled by WeatherDecider
         — it comes only from RM_MapComponent_ContagionSky's clock (see
         RM_ContagionSkyExtension below), so its frequency is ours. The
         remaining vanilla wet weathers are the storm's lulls. -->
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <RM_ContagionBloom>70</RM_ContagionBloom>
      <RainyThunderstorm>4</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>4</FoggyRain>
      <Rain>2</Rain>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Contagion.RM_ContagionSkyExtension">
        <meanDaysBetweenBurns>3</meanDaysBetweenBurns>
        <burnDurationTicks>1500~4000</burnDurationTicks>
        <tellLeadTicks>1250</tellLeadTicks>
        <extraNatives>
          <li>RM_TheUnfinished</li>
        </extraNatives>
        <armoredNatives>
          <li>RM_Scaldhide</li>
          <li>RM_Crispling</li>
        </armoredNatives>
        <leakerNatives>
          <li>RM_Scorchpod</li>
        </leakerNatives>
        <tellSinkers>
          <li>RM_Gawpsack</li>
        </tellSinkers>
        <tellRattlers>
          <li>RM_Rattlegrope</li>
        </tellRattlers>
        <!-- vanilla Ideology one-shot (audio ruling 2026-10-03: vanilla ships as final) -->
        <tellRattleSound>LeavesRustle</tellRattleSound>
        <coalescenceDef>RM_Coalescence</coalescenceDef>
        <coalescenceLongBloomTicks>90000</coalescenceLongBloomTicks>
        <coalescenceMtbDays>0.5</coalescenceMtbDays>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <wildAnimals>
      <!-- CONTAGION_RULED_CONTENT_1 Wave A, 2026-09-29: the donor AA_/AG_/GR_
           cast and RM_Sytheclaw (never admitted here; Pyrelands is its home)
           are OUT — replaced outright by the RM_ port below, per the cast
           bible's full-RM-development ruling. Commonalities are the cast
           bible §2's ruled numbers verbatim. Shorthand element form only —
           <li> silently discards a wildAnimals entry. -->
      <RM_Gawpsack>2.0</RM_Gawpsack>  <!-- gawpsack - the-eyes -->
      <RM_Scorchpod>0.85</RM_Scorchpod>  <!-- scorchpod - the-leaker -->
      <RM_BloodyMess>0.75</RM_BloodyMess>  <!-- bloody mess - the-body -->
      <RM_ContagionIkee>0.6</RM_ContagionIkee>  <!-- ikee - the-wretched-small; defName disambiguated from RM_Ikee (Stillsand's own RM_Ikee.xml collides — see the fauna file's own note and CONTAGION_IKEE_NAME_COLLISION_1) -->
      <RM_Peeper>0.5</RM_Peeper>  <!-- peeper - the-watcher-kin -->
      <RM_Ogleknot>0.3</RM_Ogleknot>  <!-- ogleknot - the eye-knot (OGLEKNOT_CREATURE_BUILD_1) -->
      <RM_Eyestinger>0.5</RM_Eyestinger>  <!-- eyestinger - the-tail -->
      <RM_Fleshsop>0.5</RM_Fleshsop>  <!-- fleshsop - the-pitiable -->
      <RM_Blisterfloat>0.5</RM_Blisterfloat>  <!-- blisterfloat - the-sower -->
      <RM_Bloodlurk>0.2</RM_Bloodlurk>  <!-- bloodlurk - the-drinker -->
      <RM_Sparkleech>0.15</RM_Sparkleech>  <!-- sparkleech - the-thieves (adult) -->
      <RM_Doublemaw>0.15</RM_Doublemaw>  <!-- doublemaw - the-pickers -->
      <RM_Meltgut>0.1</RM_Meltgut>  <!-- meltgut - the-undertaker -->
      <RM_Scaldhide>0.1</RM_Scaldhide>  <!-- scaldhide - the-basker -->
      <RM_Gnashling>0.1</RM_Gnashling>  <!-- gnashling - the-pickers -->
      <RM_Skinflap>1.2</RM_Skinflap>  <!-- skinflap - goo-bud flyer, the Bloom's confetti -->
      <RM_Sloshbelly>0.25</RM_Sloshbelly>  <!-- sloshbelly - the cistern -->
      <RM_Crispling>0.3</RM_Crispling>  <!-- crispling - the burn-line scavenger -->
      <RM_Danglemaw>0.12</RM_Danglemaw>  <!-- danglemaw - the ambusher -->
      <RM_Gorekite>0.08</RM_Gorekite>  <!-- gorekite - apex of the canopy air -->
      <RM_SparkleechGrub>0.05</RM_SparkleechGrub>  <!-- sparkleech grub - the-thieves (grub) -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <!-- CONTAGION_FLORA_PORT_1: the donor AB_* cast is OUT — replaced
           outright by the RM_ port below, per the cast bible's
           full-RM-development ruling. Commonalities are the cast bible §4's
           ruled numbers verbatim. Shorthand element form only — <li>
           silently discards a wildPlants entry. -->
      <RM_Eyebark>1.0</RM_Eyebark>  <!-- eyebark - the-canopy -->
      <RM_Lashgrass>1.0</RM_Lashgrass>  <!-- lashgrass - ground cover -->
      <RM_Bleedleaf>0.6</RM_Bleedleaf>  <!-- bleedleaf - low shrub -->
      <RM_Gorestalk>0.5</RM_Gorestalk>  <!-- gorestalk - tall columns -->
      <RM_HalfmadeTree>0.5</RM_HalfmadeTree>  <!-- halfmade tree - infection front -->
      <RM_Rattlegrope>0.4</RM_Rattlegrope>  <!-- rattlegrope - the second tell -->
      <RM_Sapblister>0.4</RM_Sapblister>  <!-- sapblister - sap/wound-sealant source -->
      <RM_BloodyFist>0.3</RM_BloodyFist>  <!-- bloody fist - seed-fist fertilizer source -->
      <RM_RustPuff MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">0.3</RM_RustPuff>  <!-- rust puff -->
      <RM_HalfmadeTreeBlighted>0.15</RM_HalfmadeTreeBlighted>  <!-- blighted halfmade tree - front-line variant -->
      <RM_Meatvine>0.35</RM_Meatvine>  <!-- meatvine - infection-front vine -->
      <RM_Toothmoss>0.3</RM_Toothmoss>  <!-- toothmoss - burn-line carpet -->
      <RM_Wombpod>0.2</RM_Wombpod>  <!-- wombpod - genome-loop host source -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>25</wildPlantRegrowDays>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
